--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [over.match.class.deduct]/1.1, [temp.deduct.call]/3: the deduction
guide formed from the constructor S(W<T> &) deduces T = int from the lvalue
w of type W<int>.  The front end found no deduction for a constructor
parameter that is a reference to a template-id ("found no match for symbol
'S', candidates are: ...", bin53): it matched the reference pattern itself
against the argument instead of the referred type ([temp.deduct.call]/3).
By value, `T &' and `T *' worked.  libstdc++ 13's
__do_vformat_to declares `_Formatting_scanner __scanner(__ctx, __fmt);'
with the constructor _Formatting_scanner(basic_format_context<_Out, _CharT>
&, basic_string_view<_CharT>), so its body was dropped (seen with
--verbosity 9 in the <format> reductions, after
cpp_function_template_default_argument_on_earlier_declaration).
test_shapes.desc: other reference and pointer parameters.  Rvalue
arguments: cpp17_ctad_constructor_rvalue_reference_to_template_id.  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
